# Purpose: Commit and check out every text file with LF line endings, on every
#          platform and whatever core.autocrlf says. The build copies files
#          from the working tree into the images (build/openssl-fips.cnf, for
#          one), so CRLF endings would change the image digests; bash also
#          cannot run a script that has them.
# Role: Git attributes, read by Git whenever it commits or checks out a file.
#       One rule covers every path: Git detects binary files itself and leaves
#       them unchanged.
* text=auto eol=lf
